/**
 * Nonfiction Hotlist: website editing kit setup.
 *
 * Builds the "NFH Website" folder that nonfictionhotlist.com is made from:
 *   00 How this works            guide for editors
 *   01 Pages/                    one Google Doc per page
 *   02 News/                     one Google Doc per news post
 *   Media/                       images the pages use
 *   Site                         Google Sheet: Pages, News, Menu, Footer, Settings
 *   Site manifest (do not edit)  the map the website reads
 *
 * How to run: script.google.com > New project > paste this file > select buildKit > Run.
 * Approve the permissions it asks for. If it stops to stay under Google's time limit, it continues
 * on its own a minute later. Running it again only fills in what's missing.
 *
 * Adding a page or a news post: add a row to the Pages or News tab of the Site sheet. Within about
 * 10 minutes (refreshKit) it gets its own Doc, linked in the row's Doc column.
 * Adding an image: drop it in Media and use [image: file name.jpg] in a page.
 *
 * Generated by scripts/kit/build-kit.js. Edit that and the template, not this file.
 */

